    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00a14704_8e097181",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/entry.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 297,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T15:36:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`transmute` is a **very** unsafe operation.\n\nIn this case, you\u0027re turning a `\u0026` into a `*mut`, changing the mutability itself, which could confuse the borrow checked and conflict with potential optimizations.\n\nFurthermore, note that you\u0027re transmuting `\u0026slices.fdt`, a reference-to-reference-to-`[u8]` into a pointer you want to be pointing to the DT (`[u8]`)... Does the compiler fold the double-`\u0026` or are you actually copying from the bytes of the `slices` structure, here?\n\nAnyway, I believe a better (and safe!) way to achieve the cast would be\n```\nslices.fdt as *mut _ as *mut u8\n```\nwhich could probably be simplified to\n```\nslices.fdt as *mut _ as *mut _\n```\nwith type deduction (I don\u0027t think the compiler would accept `slices.fdt as *mut _` but TBD).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 297,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 297,
        "endChar": 79
      },
